{
 "schema": "bt-datum-classes/1",
 "_doc": "The datum-class registry of GATE-SPEC.md Q02.1 (the census). Every data file that the page loads (found by the static scan of app/src and render/prototype/src in lib/loadlist.py) has to be in the `files` of at least one class, or the census is FAIL. `source` says where the members of the class are read from (lib/datum_scan.py): the real history layer (`layer`, dumped by q02_layer.mjs with the app's own code), a JSON path, JSONL ledgers, or every tier-bearing record of a file (`walk`). `visible` marks the classes whose values change what is seen or heard (the census of Q19.1). `validity` (`kit` or `state`) marks classes whose items need valid_from/valid_to (Q02.9) or a state_schedule. `claims` marks classes whose records carry source extracts that are re-matched in the stored text (Q02.3). The registry names no tier, source or extract: those are read from the data, never written here.",
